---
/**
 * How to say it, and the other names.
 *
 * Its own page because a person who cannot say a word will not order it, and
 * because "is nazook the same as gata" is a different search made by a
 * different person from "what is gata". The two belong together though: the
 * answer to both is one short page about the word rather than the pastry.
 * See docs/DECISIONS.md D-008.
 *
 * Which name Hakop's own household uses is left for the family to answer. It
 * is not guessed at here. See docs/HANDOVER.md section 6.
 */
import Explainer from "./_Explainer.astro";
---

<Explainer
  slug="how-to-say-it"
  seoTitle="How to say gata, and the other names"
  description="Gata is two syllables, gah-TAH, with the second one stronger. It is written as Gata in Armenian script. Some households call the same pastry nazook, and some call it kata."
>
  <div class="prose-col">
    <p class="say__lede">
      Two syllables, the second one stronger.
    </p>

    <p class="say__word">
      <span class="say__soft">gah</span>-<span class="say__stress">TAH</span>
    </p>

    <p class="say__detail">
      Written <span lang="hy" class="say__native">Գաթա</span> in Armenian.
    </p>

    <h2 class="say__names-title">Nazook, kata, gata</h2>
    <p>
      The same pastry answers to more than one name, and which one a person
      uses usually says where their family is from rather than what is in the
      tray. Nazook and kata both turn up. If you grew up with one of those
      words, this is that.
    </p>

    <div class="todo">
      <p class="todo__label">
        <span class="todo__seed" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        For the family to answer
      </p>
      <p class="todo__body">
        Which name Hakop's household uses, and how they say it, is theirs to
        tell. When they do, it goes here in their words rather than in a
        summary of them.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Explainer>

<style>
  .say__lede {
    margin-top: 1.1rem;
    font-size: var(--text-lg);
    line-height: var(--leading-snug);
    color: var(--color-crust-soft);
  }

  .say__word {
    margin-top: 0.75rem;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--text-4xl);
    line-height: 1.15;
  }

  .say__soft {
    color: var(--color-crust-soft);
  }

  /* The stressed syllable, carried by weight and colour rather than by
     setting the whole word in tracked out capitals. */
  .say__stress {
    color: var(--color-crust);
    font-weight: 700;
    border-bottom: 3px solid var(--color-eggwash);
  }

  .say__detail {
    margin-top: 0.8rem;
    color: var(--color-crust-soft);
  }

  .say__native {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    color: var(--color-eggwash-ink);
    font-size: var(--text-lg);
  }

  .say__names-title {
    margin-top: 2.25rem;
    font-size: var(--text-xl);
  }

  /* ---- Unanswered, marked as such ---- */

  .todo {
    margin-top: 1.35rem;
    padding: clamp(0.9rem, 3vw, 1.35rem);
    background-color: var(--color-paper);
    border: 2px dashed var(--color-line-strong);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
  }

  .todo__label {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.55rem;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--color-warn);
  }

  .todo__seed {
    flex: none;
    width: 8px;
    height: 5px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background-color: var(--color-warn);
    transform: rotate(-24deg);
  }

  .todo__body {
    margin-top: 0.6rem;
    color: var(--color-crust-soft);
    max-width: 58ch;
  }
</style>
